"DESIGN task: satisfy all four stories in ONE system -- no battle mode in the simulation and no mode switch that removes options. The tension: the two cons (distraction, input count under threat) pull toward filtering, while the two pros (creative battle actions, attacking scenery while exploring) require that nothing ever be filtered OUT. Candidate principle: THREAT DEMOTES, NEVER REMOVES -- a derived threat signal (co-located hostiles, computable client-side from subscribed allegiance/location/hp state, no server mode) scales sorting aggressiveness: under threat, hostile targets and combat-valid actions surface; exploration-only targets collapse into a secondary surroundings group but stay reachable; while calm, the ordering relaxes and attackable scenery ranks normally. Fast-obvious-choice rides the same signal: a maintained default focus (single hostile auto-focused; cycling when several) plus one-input attack-focus. Existing partial machinery: entity_prominence bit ranking (path/player/hp), getActionOptions per-target action validity, action hotkeys."